  "verification_contract": "Ports MUST (a) derive the same keys from the seeds, (b) byte-match the deterministic_prefix, (c) VERIFY the reference_jws signature slot under those keys - the slot is ONE base64url segment decoding to the raw 64+3309 byte concatenation; split by the constant lengths - and (d) produce their own signatures over the same prefix that also verify. Ports accepting legacy receipts must implement the dot-form split with the same component lengths. Signature bytes are not reproducible: ML-DSA signs randomised.\n\nByte-flip convention (added 24 Nov): legacy_verify_only vectors carry UNFLIPPED input_jws bytes plus a declared 'flip' {segment, byte, xor} the port applies before verification. Current-form vectors carry input_jws bytes ALREADY flipped at the recorded segment/byte (bytes_state=pre_flipped, no 'flip' key) - applying a declared flip there would undo the corruption. Read bytes as-is unless bytes_state says otherwise.",
